  "text": "proprium.ascensio-domini-epistola",
  "about": "The epistola of the formulary “Ascension of the Lord” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "The first account I made, O Theophilus, of all things which Jesus began to do and to teach, until the day on which, giving commandments through the Holy Spirit to the Apostles whom He had chosen, He was taken up. To them also He showed Himself alive after His Passion by many proofs, appearing to them for forty days and speaking of the kingdom of God. And eating with them, He commanded them not to depart from Jerusalem, but to wait for the promise of the Father, which, He said, you have heard from My mouth: for John indeed baptized with water, but you will be baptized with the Holy Spirit not many days from now. Those therefore who had come together asked Him, saying: Lord, will You at this time restore the kingdom to Israel? But He said to them: It is not for you to know the times or moments which the Father has placed in His own power; but you will receive the power of the Holy Spirit coming upon you, and you will be witnesses to Me in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and even to the uttermost part of the earth. And when He had said these things, while they looked on, He was lifted up, and a cloud received Him out of their sight. And while they were gazing into heaven as He went, behold, two men stood by them in white garments, who also said: Men of Galilee, why do you stand looking up to heaven? This Jesus, who has been taken up from you into heaven, will come in the same way as you have seen Him going into heaven.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w015", "w016"], "anchor": "w016", "gloss": "until" }, { "words": ["w022", "w023"], "anchor": "w022", "gloss": "the Holy Spirit" }, { "words": ["w026", "w027"], "anchor": "w026", "gloss": "was taken up" }, { "words": ["w075", "w076"], "anchor": "w075", "gloss": "with the Holy Spirit" }, { "words": ["w099", "w100"], "anchor": "w100", "gloss": "It is not" }, { "words": ["w116", "w117"], "anchor": "w116", "gloss": "of the Holy Spirit" }, { "words": ["w143", "w144"], "anchor": "w143", "gloss": "was lifted up" }, { "words": ["w180", "w181"], "anchor": "w180", "gloss": "has been taken up" }] }
  },
